      <p>Advertised web rates are often promotional. We look for what the operator says happens after the first months, and how much notice you get.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Rate-lock policies</h3>
      <p>Some companies advertise a lock on base rent. Others are month-to-month with a right to raise the rate. We record the public policy, not a sales pitch.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Climate vs. standard units</h3>
      <p>North Georgia summers are hot and humid. We explain when climate control is worth asking for, and what “climate-controlled” actually means at a given brand.</p>
